cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "iqforge"
abstract: >-
  A command-line tool that turns SDR captures in SigMF format into labelled,
  PyTorch-ready datasets. Windows are split at the recording level rather than
  the window level, and the tool refuses to run instead of silently falling back
  to a split that would inflate reported accuracy.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Bulut"
    given-names: "Emre"
repository-code: "https://github.com/emrefbulut/iqforge"
url: "https://github.com/emrefbulut/iqforge"
license: MIT
version: "0.2.0"
# date-released is deliberately absent until the version above is tagged, so this
# file never dates a release nobody can fetch. docs/publishing.md carries it in
# the pre-release checklist.
keywords:
  - software-defined-radio
  - sigmf
  - rf-machine-learning
  - signal-processing
  - pytorch
  - dataset
